@startuml idle-event
' Idle event handshake (docs/spec/06-operation.md, section 6.1). The slave pulls DATA low while the bus is idle
' with CLK low, the master confirms with clock pulses, and the slave releases DATA after the first falling edge
' (releasing while CLK is high would look like a STOP). The master then starts a burst.
scale 10 as 90 pixels
hide time-axis
binary "CLK" as CLK
binary "DATA" as DATA
concise "Slave" as S
concise "Master" as M

@0
CLK is low
DATA is high
S is idle
M is "idle, watches DATA"
@20
DATA is low
S is "buffer written: pulls DATA low"
@30
M is "DATA low: confirm"
@40
CLK is high
@50
CLK is low
@52
DATA is high
S is released
@60
M is "DATA high: start the burst"
@80
CLK is high
M is START
@85
DATA is low
@90
CLK is low
M is "burst"
S is "contends in the burst"
@110
S is {-}
M is {-}

CLK@40 <-> @50 : one clock pulse
@enduml
